Where we went wrong
with the Farmington case...

624
00:40:30,962 --> 00:40:32,624
What could we have
done differently, Dad?

625
00:40:33,431 --> 00:40:36,026
Oh, I wasn't talking
about the case.

626
00:40:36,200 --> 00:40:40,695
I was talking about,
uh, you and me.

627
00:40:41,406 --> 00:40:43,568
You've come to a
conclusion, counselor?

628
00:40:44,676 --> 00:40:47,942
Yeah. Um...

629
00:40:49,080 --> 00:40:53,575
I have a problem recognizing

630
00:40:53,751 --> 00:40:58,587
that you're a grown woman
with your own way of doing things.

631
00:40:59,624 --> 00:41:02,287
- I know that, Dad.
- Yeah.

632
00:41:02,460 --> 00:41:05,157
- So if you wanna drop my case...
- You want me to drop the case?

633
00:41:05,330 --> 00:41:08,630
No, no. No, I'm...
Look, I need you.

634
00:41:09,000 --> 00:41:11,026
Good, I'm glad.

635
00:41:11,202 --> 00:41:14,695
Because one piece
of advice I did listen to:

636
00:41:15,039 --> 00:41:16,769
Always finish what you start.

637
00:41:23,681 --> 00:41:25,547
Wait a second.

638
00:41:26,784 --> 00:41:29,686
- Did you see that?
- What?

639
00:41:36,294 --> 00:41:37,626
That.

640
00:41:39,263 --> 00:41:42,461
How has the pain been since
