Maybe your lovely new
wife encouraged you.

680
00:44:09,147 --> 00:44:11,810
Uh, uh...

681
00:44:11,983 --> 00:44:13,713
- Oh, no.
- Oh, I'm not saying your wife

682
00:44:13,885 --> 00:44:15,080
had anything to do with it.

683
00:44:15,253 --> 00:44:18,189
I mean, a woman would have to
be crazy to let her husband go out

684
00:44:18,356 --> 00:44:22,384
and deliberately disable
himself for money.

685
00:44:24,562 --> 00:44:27,828
But that's what you
did, isn't it, Mr. Fuqua?

686
00:44:28,232 --> 00:44:30,292
You deliberately fell
down my client's stairs,

687
00:44:30,468 --> 00:44:35,270
hoping you would at least appear to
be injured badly enough to be set for life,

688
00:44:35,973 --> 00:44:38,875
at my client's expense.

689
00:44:42,613 --> 00:44:43,911
Well, Mr. Fuqua?

690
00:44:49,487 --> 00:44:52,013
"We, the jury, in the
above entitled action,

691
00:44:52,190 --> 00:44:56,423
return the following special verdict
on the questions presented to us.

692
00:44:56,594 --> 00:44:59,393
One: Was the defendant,
Benjamin Matlock,

693
00:44:59,564 --> 00:45:02,557
negligent in the maintenance
of his front porch?

694
00:45:02,733 --> 00:45:04,224
Yes.

695
00:45:04,402 --> 00:45:07,167
Two: Was the
defendant's negligence

696
00:45:07,338 --> 00:45:11,002
a proximate cause of
the injury to Mr. Fuqua?

697
00:45:11,175 --> 00:45:12,438
No."

698
00:45:12,610 --> 00:45:14,511
That being the case,

699
00:45:14,679 --> 00:45:17,274
Mr. Matlock is not
liable for any damages.

700
00:45:17,448 --> 00:45:20,418
Thank you, ladies and
gentlemen. You are excused.

701
00:45:20,585 --> 00:45:22,076
This court is adjourned.

702
00:45:33,497 --> 00:45:35,090
That was some work, Leanne.

703
00:45:35,266 --> 00:45:37,963
That poor guy came up against
